# Project Conventions

Refer to `CONVENTIONS.md` at the workspace root for the full specification.

## Workspace Layout

Projects are organized into category directories:
- `Research/` — Active projects (code + paper), private
- `Publish/` — Submitted/published papers, private
- `Public/` — Open-source code releases
- `Experimental/` — Exploratory projects, private
- `Personal/` — Non-research files, private

GitHub Organization: `huwei-research`. Repo name = local folder name.

## Project Structure

Research/Experimental projects must have: `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `paper/`, `codes/`.
Every independent repository must have a project-local `AGENTS.md`; start new
projects from `.agents/templates/project_agents_template.md` in the
workspace-meta repository.
Inside `codes/`: `core/`, `solvers/`, `problems/`, `experiments/`, `tests/`, `utils/`, `scripts/`, `results/`, `plans/`.

## Naming Rules

- Repository names: uppercase acronym (BUPTR, MATRO) or PascalCase (MemOTRO, SelfCorrecting)
- Internal directories: `lowercase_snake_case` (e.g., `bup_newuoa/`, `dfo_tr/`)
- Python files: `lowercase_snake_case.py`
- Solver main: `{algorithm}.py`; versions: `{algorithm}_v{N}.py`
- Test files: `test_{module}.py`
- LaTeX submission: `{project}_{journal}_submission.tex`
- LaTeX draft: `{project}_paper_v{major}_{minor}.tex`
- Exploratory scripts: prefix with `_` (e.g., `_test_v7_quick.py`)
- Figures: `snake_case.pdf` in `paper/figures/main/` or `paper/figures/supplementary/`

## Python Style

- PEP 8, line length 100, 4-space indent
- NumPy-style docstrings on public APIs
- Imports: stdlib / third-party / local (blank-line separated)
- Classes: `PascalCase`; functions/variables: `snake_case`; constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`

## Cross-Platform (CRITICAL)

- ALWAYS use `pathlib.Path` for paths, NEVER hardcode `\` or `/`
- sys.path setup: `_CODES_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[N]`
- Create dirs with `Path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)`
- When passing paths to libraries (matplotlib, pandas): use `str(path)`
- Every project must have `.gitattributes` with `* text=auto eol=lf`

## File Placement

- New solvers go in `codes/solvers/{algorithm_name}/`
- New experiments go in `codes/experiments/{benchmarks|ablation|analysis|research|paper}/`
- Formal results go in `codes/results/paper/{experiment_name}/` with `REPORT.md`
- Scratch results go in `codes/results/scratch/` (gitignored)
- Helper scripts go in `codes/scripts/`
- Plans and checklists go in `codes/plans/`

## Git: What to Track

- TRACK: `.py`, `.csv`, `.json`, `.xls`, `.xlsx`, `.md`, `.tex`, `.txt`
- DO NOT TRACK: LaTeX artifacts, `.venv/`, `__pycache__/`, `codes/results/scratch/`
- Exception: `paper/**/*.pdf` and `paper/**/*.png` ARE tracked
- Figures in `codes/results/` are NOT tracked (regenerated from CSV)

## Results Storage

- `codes/results/paper/` — formal results for publication (tracked, REPORT.md required)
- `codes/results/archive/` — old formal results (tracked)
- `codes/results/scratch/` — temporary/debug runs (gitignored)
- Timestamp format: `YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_{experiment_name}/`

## Experiment Structure

- Fixed seeds: `SEEDS = [42, 123, 7, 256, 999]`
- Default opts: `{"max_eval": 3000, "rhobeg": 1.0, "rhoend": 1e-8}`
- Success metric: More-Wild relative error
- Save raw data to CSV; figures generated separately and not committed

## Versioning

- Paper versions: `v{major}_{minor}` in filename
- Code versions: Git tags `v{major}.{minor}.{patch}`
- Tag at submission milestones: `v1.0.0-siopt-submission`

## Cloning & Syncing

- Org: `https://github.com/huwei-research/`
- Clone into category dirs: `git clone .../BUPTR.git Research/BUPTR`
- After clone: `cd <project>/codes && python -m venv .venv && pip install -r requirements.txt`
- Regenerate figures: `python scripts/replot.py`
- Daily: `git pull --ff-only` before working, `git add -A && git commit && git push` after
